02:13:07.690 --> 02:13:18.257
[SPEAKER_00]: carefully after tests or by repacking they are damaged after a very short time already. And that didn't happen 10 years ago when the fabric

02:13:18.297 --> 02:13:29.141
[SPEAKER_00]: was double as strong as it is right now. That's one part of the story. Another part is that in the past 20, 30 years, there was always

02:13:29.921 --> 02:13:41.365
[SPEAKER_00]: development. And after 10 years, after five years, after 10 years, one could say, okay, the new designs are better. Now it's time for a

02:13:41.445 --> 02:13:56.134
[SPEAKER_00]: replacement. And the third thing is that I know that DHV did once, but that's a long time ago. They did once, did a load test of older reserve

02:13:56.194 --> 02:14:08.042
[SPEAKER_00]: parachutes, 10, 15 years old from hang gliders. Most of them exploded in the first drop test. One could see the strength of the fabric really lost

02:14:08.282 --> 02:14:17.755
[SPEAKER_00]: during that time. It's like climbing ropes with climbing equipment, carabiners who have the same rules. I think it's also to ensure the

02:14:17.795 --> 02:14:26.180
[SPEAKER_00]: designers, the manufacturers from liability stuff. Makes sense. But how do you guys decide that this reserve is not fly worthy anymore or is it

02:14:26.240 --> 02:14:34.545
[SPEAKER_02]: reaching that stage? Are there visible signs or is there a porosity test and the usual ones? First we do the visible tests on the paraglider. We

02:14:34.565 --> 02:14:50.958
[SPEAKER_00]: check risers, lines, swing. canopy we hang it up in our room and we have very strong lights from the other side so we can walk around and see if

02:14:51.038 --> 02:15:01.500
[SPEAKER_00]: there are damages the history is important we want to know how many openings this reserve had how many went into water we have a database

02:15:01.540 --> 02:15:13.653
[SPEAKER_00]: from our customer on the porosity side It is really difficult. Most of the porosimeters out there, most of the technical gear is not able to

02:15:14.634 --> 02:15:24.437
[SPEAKER_00]: measure the porosity because it's too porous. You cannot measure. There is a textile clock, an old one from Kretschmer. That's the only one

02:15:24.477 --> 02:15:35.122
[SPEAKER_00]: who can measure. They're very expensive. New instruments are like 10,000 euros. Universities do have such equipment. but not in our

02:15:35.182 --> 02:15:48.967
[SPEAKER_00]: industry. And we also cannot compare because we have no experience from this kind of things. But I would say so far, the tests, strength-wise,

02:15:49.627 --> 02:16:05.135
[SPEAKER_00]: they are really good. And the experience tells us we are in a good way. I'm not sure for the ultralight equipment, no. Unfortunately, Sometimes

02:16:05.656 --> 02:16:20.582
[SPEAKER_00]: the industry needs accidents before they change to anything. I don't hope we have to see that, but it could be the case in the next few years.

02:16:21.542 --> 02:16:30.726
[SPEAKER_02]: Sorry to hear that. Keeping our fingers crossed, that is not the case. But from a consumer's perspective, what are the best ways to maintain a

02:16:31.606 --> 02:16:43.503
[SPEAKER_02]: reserve parachute and take care of it? Keep it and care it like your baby. Don't sit on it. Humidity is a problem. Don't put the harness into wet

02:16:43.763 --> 02:16:53.088
[SPEAKER_00]: grass. When you land in water, don't try it on the sun. Don't, you know, ground handling. Don't ground handle your reserve parachute. I get

02:16:53.268 --> 02:17:02.972
[SPEAKER_00]: always shocked when I see All our aerobatic pilots drying their Beamers III after they landed in the water on Lake Guadalcee, they ground handle

02:17:03.032 --> 02:17:12.939
[SPEAKER_00]: it. You destroy a glider within minutes. Even on a grassy slope, you can destroy the fabric within two or three moves. The friction with the

02:17:12.959 --> 02:17:20.321
[SPEAKER_00]: ground basically takes away... No, not the friction, but also on the grass, you have sharp grass when it's cutted fresh. I see. when you step

02:17:20.401 --> 02:17:30.789
[SPEAKER_00]: on it when it slides on it can be a really a fabric killer right away so really take care about your reserve parachute it's your life insurance

02:17:30.849 --> 02:17:42.478
[SPEAKER_00]: it's your last chance it's really an important part of your equipment i'm guilty of that because i've gone out and aired my reserve before

02:17:42.538 --> 02:17:50.478
[SPEAKER_00]: repacking you just inflate it and then it does drag a little bit on the grass here and there yeah Don't do that with light fabric. When you hang

02:17:50.539 --> 02:18:01.601
[SPEAKER_00]: it up in the room with strong lights, you will see immediately what you destroyed. I can share some pictures later on in our workspace. It's

02:18:01.721 --> 02:18:14.192
[SPEAKER_00]: really, sometimes it's difficult to decide when it's a two or three year old modern reserve parachute. Should we still fold this one or tell the

02:18:14.212 --> 02:18:22.859
[SPEAKER_00]: guy we have a problem? I know what happens on the load tests at the certification. Over 90% of the shoots are failing on the first drop. We

02:18:22.899 --> 02:18:31.085
[SPEAKER_00]: are limited with the light fabric. These damages are not visible to the naked eye. It's only when you put bright lights and those kind of things.

02:18:31.926 --> 02:18:39.070
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, when you have an understanding of all those things. so how does airing out a reserve look like let's give a solution to the listeners

02:18:39.750 --> 02:18:48.994
[SPEAKER_00]: what when you have to air your reserve out before sending it for repack how do you do that yeah first thing most important thing put yourself in

02:18:49.034 --> 02:19:01.045
[SPEAKER_00]: with the harness into a simulator throw your harness to see if it opens avoid every single contact with sharp edges so try to do it indoor in the

02:19:01.105 --> 02:19:14.847
[SPEAKER_00]: gym area or with a man with a school where they have a large free space and then take your glider take your shoot on the lines together hang it up for

02:19:15.067 --> 02:19:26.749
[SPEAKER_00]: 48 hours in the humidity must be good it shouldn't be too dry because of electrostatic charging you will feel it immediately in winter time

02:19:26.769 --> 02:19:38.164
[SPEAKER_00]: this is a problem when you have strong heating going on in a room when the air is very dry the fabric charges itself is electrostatic so it's the

02:19:38.204 --> 02:19:47.286
[SPEAKER_00]: panels are sticking together ah so they're not airing out properly yeah okay so you really then you need a little bit you need then you can spray a

02:19:47.326 --> 02:20:00.466
[SPEAKER_00]: little bit water into the air and keep it 48 or even longer if you have time it was compressed the material so keep it open hanged up in a room Don't

02:20:00.506 --> 02:20:15.630
[SPEAKER_00]: stand on it. And then we pack it flat place. Also here again, no sharp items around. Be careful. No ground handling with your reserve. No

02:20:15.750 --> 02:20:26.313
[SPEAKER_00]: ground handling at all. This is absolute no-go. Take your old reserve. Instead of slowing away, go ground handle with your old reserve, but not

02:20:26.353 --> 02:20:33.996
[SPEAKER_00]: with your current reserve. This is a bad idea. If you want to see how strong you are. No, but the reason why I'm asking this is there's so many

02:20:34.036 --> 02:20:42.759
[SPEAKER_02]: videos on YouTube where SIE can show the reserves being cleared out on the side of the lake. I attempt to write comments in there, but I stopped.

02:20:43.599 --> 02:20:53.403
[SPEAKER_00]: Because people think then, oh, the high adventure has a problem because they're using bad material and so on. I stopped. And when I see people

02:20:53.423 --> 02:21:03.093
[SPEAKER_00]: ground handling with light material, I always think, oh, that's good for the market. pretty soon a new reserve parachute yeah stupidity has

02:21:03.153 --> 02:21:11.535
[SPEAKER_02]: no bounds but okay so light parachute is definitely a no-no but what about a regular parachute what happens can you stretch the lines as well

